> Similar issues with Directional Spatial, particularly {fa'a}. I suggest
> "When tagging a sumti, the event is oriented toward that sumti" to make
> it clear that only the location of the tagged sumti is relevant, not its
> own orientation. Unless something else was actually meant, in which case
> it's actively misleading.

Indeed the orientation of the tagged sumti is completely irrelevant. I 
wouldn't have thought it is relevant from the definition, but if there 
is potential for confusion then it should be improved.

How about:

"When tagging a sumti, the sumti specifies that the event is oriented 
toward the location of the sumti."

> Likewise, for {to'o}, "When tagging a sumti, the event is oriented away
> from that sumti."

Or:

"When tagging a sumti, the sumti specifies that the event is oriented 
away from the location of the sumti."

But feel free to suggest something else.

